# Kept out of the image that deploy/fly/Dockerfile builds; the build context is the repository's
# root. No key file belongs in the repository folder; .near-credentials is listed in case one is
# made there by mistake.
.git
**/target
**/node_modules
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/data
**/.near-credentials
# Local agent state, never tracked.
**/.superpowers

# Further guards: these mirror the secret and wallet patterns of the root .gitignore.
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.asc
**/*.gpg
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/*.keystore
**/secrets
**/credentials
**/*credentials*.json
**/*secret*
**/*.mnemonic
**/*mnemonic*
**/*.wallet
**/wallets
**/keystore

# The build context is the working tree, untracked files included: an env file or a phrase file
# under any other name stays out too, such as one that keys from-seed --gateway-env wrote.
**/*.env
**/*phrase*

# These mirror the root .gitignore's local agent and editor state. Local settings can quote a
# command line, and NEAR's Agent Skills carry no licence, so neither is redistributed.
**/CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.local.*
.claude/skills/near-*
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/*.swp
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# These mirror the root .gitignore's build, dependency and test output. A log can quote an endpoint.
**/dist
**/build
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv
**/*.log
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/.cache
